# CURSOR COMPOSER 2 — CVPASSPORT PROTOCOL

## PROJECT IDENTITY
- Stack: React CRA (NOT Next.js), Supabase, Vercel Hobby
- Global CSS: src/index.css ONLY. src/App.css is NOT imported — do not touch it.
- PDF engine: Puppeteer + @sparticuz/chromium-min, linear-gradient body hack, PAGE_HEIGHT 1027px. Never refactor this.
- Templates: Template1 to Template14. File pattern: src/Template[N][Name].js + src/serverLib/template[N]Builder.js
- Deployment: Vercel. Never suggest npm audit fix --force.

## NO-FLY ZONE — DO NOT TOUCH
- Supabase RLS policies. Never modify .sql files or suggest disabling RLS.
- api/generate-pdf.js PDF architecture. No coordinate or layout changes without explicit user instruction.
- api/cover-letter.js payment gate. The Anthropic API must only fire post-payment.
- Pricing logic in Pricing.jsx and UpgradeModal.jsx.
- Auth flow in authUtils.js and App.js auth sections.
- .env variables. Never log, hardcode, or expose keys anywhere.
- src/coverLetterDataBank.generated.js — must stay tracked in git, never ignored.
- STRUCTURE: Never move or rename files in src/ or api/. Keep Template[N][Name].js flat naming exactly as-is.
- PDF SYNTAX: Never modernize or update Puppeteer syntax. @sparticuz/chromium-min is version-locked. If it works, leave it.

## CODING STANDARDS
- Functional React components only. No class components.
- Never delete props without checking all children that consume them.
- Never upgrade libraries. Use versions already in package.json.
- No transition: all — use explicit properties with cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1).
- No purple anywhere in UI. Ever.
- Btn-primary: white bg, black text, 12px radius.
- Design tokens: --bg-page:#0A0A0A, --bg-surface:#141414, --bg-elevated:#1C1C1C, --text-primary:#FFF, --text-secondary:#A0A0A0, --border-default:#2A2A2A.
- useEffect: never add dependencies to fix a warning without checking for infinite loop risk first.

## AUTOMATION (YOLO MODE)
- You have permission to run npm run lint and npm run build autonomously.
- If build fails, read terminal output and fix immediately. Do not commit on failure.
- Only commit after npm run build passes successfully.
- Commit format: "feat: [description]" or "fix: [description]". No permission needed if build passes.
- PS-EXECUTION: If any terminal command returns a non-zero exit code, STOP. Fix the error before running the next command. No skipping.

## POWERSHELL WARNING
- No && command chaining. Run commands one at a time.